<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Questions therapists ask first</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>Are you accepting new LPC Associates?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>One supervision spot opens in spring 2027. Supervision is capped
      deliberately, so it is worth booking a consult before a spot opens rather than after.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Can I do EMDR consultation without being supervised by you?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Yes. Consultation is separate from supervision and open to any licensed therapist
      trained in EMDR, at $185 an hour online. LPC Associates under Reem's supervision get
      individual EMDR consults at no additional cost.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do I have to be in Texas?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>For LPC supervision, yes: the supervised experience requirement is set by the Texas
      Behavioral Health Executive Council and applies to Texas LPC Associates. EMDR consultation
      is a peer professional relationship rather than clinical care, so it is not limited to
      Texas, though you should check what your own board expects.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What is the first step?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>A free thirty-minute consult by Zoom or phone. For supervision, applications then need
      a CV, three professional references, and answers to the seven questions listed on the
      supervision page.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
  {% include "partials/faq-more.njk" %}
</section>

